course: dictionary
lesson: 12753
title: Durability: how long things last
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Durability is how long something lasts and how well it stands up to use, wear and damage. You can find its meaning in the words around it. «The shoes were tough enough to survive a whole year of playground games.» Tough and survive are clues: the shoes kept working through lots of hard use, so durability must mean how well they last.
explain: The adjective is durable. «Her new bag has great durability.» Try your meaning in the sentence: «Her new bag has great how-long-it-lasts-and-stands-up-to-wear.» It still makes sense, so you have understood it.
explain: In science and design, durability is a property of a material, like strength or flexibility. Engineers think about it before they build anything. «The team chose steel for the bridge because of its durability.» Steel is strong and lasts for years, so the choice makes sense.
fact: Durability is a noun, and it is uncountable: you say «good durability», not «a durability».
fact: Durable means lasting a long time and standing up to wear: «durable boots» can survive many winters.
fact: A durability test checks how long something lasts when it is used or knocked about.
fact: Materials are chosen for durability: a school bag made of tough nylon has more durability than a thin paper one.
fact: Durable goods are things like furniture and fridges that are built to last for years.
exercise: «The shoes were tough enough to survive a whole year of playground games.» What does durability mean? | How heavy a bag feels | *How long something lasts and stands up to wear | How bright a colour looks | How fast something can run
exercise: Which word is the adjective form of durability? | Darken | Duration | *Durable
exercise: Which material would be best for a school bag that must last many years? | Wet cardboard | *Strong, tough nylon | Tissue paper | Thin paper
test: «The bridge was built for durability, so it could carry heavy lorries for decades.» What does built for durability suggest? | Built to be taken apart each week | *Built to last and stand up to heavy use | Built quickly and cheaply | Built to be painted bright colours
test: Which sentence uses durability correctly? | *The durability of the tent kept it standing through three storms. | Durability is a yellow colour. | The durability of the sunny afternoon was lovely. | I durability my shoes every morning.
exam: Why might a designer test a bridge for durability? | To make it a bright colour | *To find out how long it will last under heavy use | To see if it can float
